From f553fd7f84e70b39c37beb990aed2447ee089441 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chunleiding <128339845+chunleiding@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 12:15:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix: support the current harness session API and
 surface-replace shape
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three incompatibilities with current DeepSeek Harness releases:

1. `session.events` no longer exists. The log is private and published
   through `eventAt(seq)` and `snapshotEvents(from, to)`. Added
   `src/session-compat.js` (prefers the accessors, falls back to the legacy
   array) and routed all ten read sites in index/region/recall/search
   through it, so both harness generations work.

2. A replace `surfaceOp` is now `{ op, startSeq, endSeq }` — a backend that
   writes `{ op, start, end }` fails surface validation, which surfaced as
   "session event "user/message" carries an invalid replace surfaceOp".

3. Seeded `assistant/message` events now require settlement fields
   (`turn`, `step`, `stream`); the fixtures and the two test-side event
   reads were updated to match.

Verified against @deepseek-ai/dsh 0.1.5-rc.1: 99/99 tests pass.
